        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ai): match reasoning efforts case-insensitively without lowering provider values",
        "body": "Related: #102908\nAlternative to #102958\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users or plugin/catalog authors who provide canonical OpenAI-compatible reasoning effort values with mixed casing, such as `HIGH` or `XHIGH`, can have the request miss the supported-effort list and fall through to a different effort.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe resolver now folds only canonical OpenAI-owned reasoning effort names case-insensitively before lookup. Provider-native compat values remain exactly as configured, including mixed-case mapped API labels, so this avoids the compatibility risk called out on #102958 and preserves exact provider-native `reasoningEffortMap` outputs.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers get the intended reasoning effort even when canonical effort values are written with different casing. Custom provider integrations can still return provider-specific mapped effort labels without OpenClaw lowercasing those payload values.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs packages/ai/src/providers/openai-reasoning-effort.test.ts` - passed, 13 tests\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --write --threads=1 packages/ai/src/providers/openai-reasoning-effort.ts packages/ai/src/providers/openai-reasoning-effort.test.ts` - completed\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD -- packages/ai/src/providers/openai-reasoning-effort.ts packages/ai/src/providers/openai-reasoning-effort.test.ts` - passed\n- Previous single autoreview round for the draft branch was clean; not repeated after this narrow review-comment repair to stay within the draft PR guardrail.\n- `node_modules/.bin/tsx - < temporary proof script` - passed, using a loopback OpenAI-compatible `/v1/chat/completions` endpoint through `createOpenAICompletionsTransportStreamFn()` plus the Responses request builder. Redacted payload proof:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"chatCompletionsMixedCaseCanonical\": {\n    \"requestPath\": \"/v1/chat/completions\",\n    \"inputReasoning\": \" XHIGH \",\n    \"capturedReasoningEffort\": \"xhigh\"\n  },\n  \"chatCompletionsProviderNativeMap\": {\n    \"requestPath\": \"/v1/chat/completions\",\n    \"inputReasoning\": \"HIGH\",\n    \"compatSupportedReasoningEfforts\": [\"ProviderDefault\"],\n    \"compatReasoningEffortMap\": { \"high\": \"ProviderDefault\" },\n    \"capturedReasoningEffort\": \"ProviderDefault\"\n  },\n  \"chatCompletionsCanonicalLookingProviderNativeMap\": {\n    \"requestPath\": \"/v1/chat/completions\",\n    \"inputReasoning\": \"HIGH\",\n    \"compatSupportedReasoningEfforts\": [\"LOW\", \"MEDIUM\", \"HIGH\"],\n    \"compatReasoningEffortMap\": { \"high\": \"HIGH\" },\n    \"capturedReasoningEffort\": \"HIGH\"\n  },\n  \"responsesMixedCaseCanonical\": {\n    \"inputReasoningEffort\": \" XHIGH \",\n    \"capturedReasoningEffort\": \"xhigh\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nRemote proof note: Blacksmith Testbox was unavailable locally because the `blacksmith` executable is missing, and Crabbox is blocked here by a missing configured coordinator. This PR uses the documented narrow Codex-worktree local fallback for the focused unit test and loopback request-path proof.",
